Route Data Structure:

Column	                        Description
demandID	                    Identifier for the demand or commodity. Each unique value represents a specific product flow requirement.
pathID	                        Unique route identifier. Each route describes a distinct combination of legs serving the same demand.
originID	                    Origin location ID (typically a vendor).
dest1, dest2, dest3, finalDest	Intermediate and final destination nodes that define the sequence of the route.
arc1, arc2, arc3	            Leg (arc) identifiers used to connect to lane data. Each arc represents a transportation link between two consecutive nodes.
arc1_type, arc2_type, arc3_type	Type of movement for each arc (e.g., Vendor→LMD, Vendor→FC, FC→LMD).
arc1_dist, arc2_dist, arc3_dist	Distance (in miles) traveled for each arc. Zero values indicate the absence of that arc for shorter routes.
varCost	                        Handling or variable cost associated with the route (e.g., cost per pound or per-mile handling).
wgt	                            Total shipment weight in pounds for this route.
pathDist	                    Total route distance, equal to the sum of arc distances.
arcs	                        Number of arcs (legs) that make up the route. Single-arc routes are direct; multi-arc routes include intermediate stops.
directDist	                    Direct (origin-to-finalDest) distance if the shipment were sent without intermediate nodes.
sales	                        Total sales value of the commodity being shipped on the route.
cogs	                        Cost of goods sold associated with the commodity.
fixedTT	                    Fixed portion of the route’s travel time, expressed in days.
current_ODT	                    Currently assigned origin–destination terminal (ODT) or configuration.
transitMode	                    Mode of the final inbound leg to last-mile delivery (e.g., TL = Truckload, LTL = Less-Than-Truckload).
w_hat	                        Allowed waiting time for this route (days), typically computed as LT_upper_bound − fixed transit time.
dirMode	                        Mode of the equivalent direct route (numeric code; 0 if not direct).
dirCost	                        Cost of the direct route (zero if no direct option).
dirFreq	                        Frequency or number of dispatches for the direct route (zero if not available).


Lane Data Structure:

Column	        Description
arcID	        Unique identifier for each leg (arc). Each arc connects a specific origin and destination pair.
mode	        Shipment mode indicator: 0 = TL (Truckload); 1–3 = LTL (Less-Than-Truckload) categories. (arcID + mode defines a lane.)
originID	    Origin node ID.
originType	    Type of the origin node: VND = Vendor, FC = Fulfillment Center.
destID	        Destination node ID.
destType	    Type of the destination node: FC = Fulfillment Center, LMD = Last-Mile Delivery center.
distance	    Distance between the origin and destination for this arc (miles).
minWgt	        Minimum shipment weight allowed for this mode (pounds).
maxWgt	        Maximum shipment weight capacity for this mode (pounds).
varCost	        Variable cost per pound for shipment on this lane (applicable for certain LTL modes).
fixedCost	    Fixed dispatch cost for one shipment on this lane (independent of weight).
transitTime	    Estimated travel/transit time (days) for this lane and mode. LTL modes typically show longer transit times than TL.


Conversion Rate Data Structure:

Column      Description
ODT         Lead time (days) / Origin–Destination Terminal lead-time bucket (as represented in the conversion data).
prediction  Percentage (or fraction) of customers expected to purchase given that lead time (i.e., conversion probability).


Distance Matrix Data Structure:

Column              Description
locationID1         ID of the first location (numeric identifier).
locationType1       Node type for the first location. Allowed values: VND (Vendor), FC (Fulfillment Center), LMD (Last-Mile Delivery).
locationID2         ID of the second location (numeric identifier).
locationType2       Node type for the second location. Allowed values: VND, FC, LMD.
distance            Distance (miles) between locationID1 and locationID2 (e.g., great-circle or network distance).

